    <bodyText>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "blocks": {
    "contentData": [],
    "settingsData": [],
    "expose": [],
    "layout": {}
  },
  "markup": "\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg data-udi=\u0022umb://media/02918ce601c64f89a1a5808544950536\u0022 src=\u0022?rmode=max\u0026amp;width=900\u0026amp;height=476\u0026amp;hmac=ff3122a1c30f1acbed39882cd09abe297c5fa99aa96bde36d89bda428bf5679e\u0022 alt=\u0022Holly Roddfield\u0022 width=\u0022900\u0022 height=\u0022476\u0022\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cbr\u003ENeighboring residents and businesses have been notified of this activity, and access will remain open during construction.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe closures are part of ongoing work related to the creation of a reclaimed water pipeline from the City\u2019s Oso Water Reclamation Plant to its Greenwood Water Reclamation Plant. This water is intended for use by Valero, which will build its own infrastructure to use it, reducing demand on potable water reserves.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis strategic project is a significant step towards enhancing the city\u0027s water sustainability and infrastructure.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESafety remains a top priority, so motorists are advised to use alternative routes to avoid delays, remain aware of the work zone, and follow posted signs.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe City of Corpus Christi is committed to projects that maintain or improve streets and infrastructure for every city resident, business, and visitor.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFor more information, media representatives can contact Beth Becerra, Public Information Officer, at \u003Ca data-router-slot=\u0022disabled\u0022 href=\u0022mailto:elizabethb@CorpusChristiTX.gov\u0022 type=\u0022external\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003Eelizabethb@CorpusChristiTX.gov\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E or (361) 826-1693.\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
    </bodyText>
    <introText>
      <Value><![CDATA[Beginning Thursday, September 3, a section of Holly Road between Toben Drive and Rodd Field Road will be closed while construction continues on a water pipeline for reclaimed water. The street closures will continue through Friday, October 16.]]></Value>
    </introText>
    <publicationDate>
      <Value><![CDATA[2026-09-03T09:02:38]]></Value>
    </publicationDate>
  </Properties>
